<p>The Milan-Cortina 2026 Winter Paralympics opened with a ceremony at Verona’s Arena in Italy, bringing athletes together to compete across six sports. The mood mixed celebration with visible tension. Russia’s national flag appeared during the opening ceremony, drawing boos from some spectators in the stadium. Ukraine and six other nations boycotted the ceremony in response, turning the Games’ first night into a diplomatic flashpoint as well as a sporting one.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/S8-H3XjkZmMuLrCcc3hQq5x2HFIahbRrMyy9Dm3C4bQfMSUFkImttuzi7wWhZxT-q1m06FrhJNZ-hhYpBeB4xh627JvB-4k4YeS7O-9q92lp8r_Se327R3Slp93NvV-mySEf0bd55IciDl1a4zP-2VqwdGBJlZQBhZ9MIU0st933wDrPz5MBBhzjyvmfDJUXOAXXttItigfX7KnNjczELELx' alt='Two Russian athletes, center, and Russian officials participated in the opening ceremony of the Winter Paralympics in Verona, Italy.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Boycott details: Ukraine led a boycott of the opening ceremony, joined by six other nations, after Russia paraded its national flag.</li><li>Delegation presence: The Hindu reported that four members of the Russian delegation represented the country on stage in bright red uniforms during the parade.</li><li>Games scale: PBS highlighted the Games’ scale, noting a record number of athletes and medals.</li><li>Sports on schedule: Competition spans six sports: para alpine skiing, para biathlon, para cross-country skiing, para ice hockey, para snowboard, and wheelchair curling.</li><li>Host setting: Verona’s Arena hosted the opening ceremony, with Milan and Cortina d’Ampezzo serving as the Games’ host sites.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ukraine and boycotting nations: Ukraine led a boycott of the opening ceremony, joined by six other nations, after Russia paraded its national flag. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/06/world/europe/2026-paralympics-russia-doping-ukraine-boycott.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Spectators at the opening ceremony: Some spectators booed as Russia’s contingent was introduced. Coverage also noted that the country was represented on stage by four delegation members wearing bright red uniforms. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/sport/russian-flag-returns-as-milan-cortina-winter-paralympics-open-amid-iran-war-and-boycott/article70714770.ece'>The Hindu</a>, <a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/sports/article/2026/03/07/milan-cortina-winter-paralympics-officially-open-amid-controversial-return-of-russia_6751181_9.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Event organizers and broadcasters: Coverage highlighted the Games’ scale, pointing to a record number of athletes and medals as competition begins. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/the-2026-winter-paralympics-have-begun-here-are-the-6-sports-athletes-are-competing-in'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/sport/russian-flag-returns-as-milan-cortina-winter-paralympics-open-amid-iran-war-and-boycott/article70714770.ece'>Russian flag returns as Milan Cortina Winter Paralympics open amid Iran war and boycott</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/06/world/europe/2026-paralympics-russia-doping-ukraine-boycott.html'>Russia Gets Silent Treatment in Paralympics Return</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/sports/article/2026/03/07/milan-cortina-winter-paralympics-officially-open-amid-controversial-return-of-russia_6751181_9.html'>Milan-Cortina Winter Paralympics officially open amid controversial return of Russia</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/the-2026-winter-paralympics-have-begun-here-are-the-6-sports-athletes-are-competing-in'>The 2026 Winter Paralympics have begun. Here are the 6 sports athletes are competing in</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://apnews.com/article/paralympics-milan-cortina-opening-ceremony-russian-flag-e791cf0241cf42fd919f80ec816f5b01'>The opening ceremony of the Winter Paralympics in Milan and Cortina d&#x